    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Filipiñana"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This bold debut, set over the course of one sweltering day, follows a 17-year-old working as a ‘tee-girl’ at a golf club."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/ivan-and-hadoum-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Iván & Hadoum"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ian de la Rosa’s debut, set in a vast greenhouse in southern Spain, is a tender love story that finds newly promoted Iván falling for co-worker Hadoum."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/our-share-of-sand-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Our Share of Sand"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Shalini Adnani’s poignant coming-of-age drama presents a unique perspective on India’s gaping class inequality, child labour and the deep corruption underpinning a family’s economic status."
    }
